# Counterfactual: the income-security supplement rule deleted
#
# Remove the one rule that concludes the supplement from a contribution record
# and an independent adjudicated event. The supplement disappears; the floor,
# personhood, and the guarantee route's own conclusion are exactly what they
# were, which is what makes the loss attributable to the one line.
:expect-pins 4
pay(Oke, Contribution, Carrier, SchemeA).
authorized(Assessor, InsuranceAdjudicator, Oke).
observe(Assessor, Illness, Oke, SchemeA).
? insure(Carrier, Oke, Illness).
# => FALSE
# The guarantee rule is a separate line and still derives on insolvency.
observe(Court, CarrierInsolvency, Carrier, SchemeA).
? insure(PublicGuarantee, Oke, Illness).
# => TRUE
# The floor never depended on the deleted line.
? entitled(Adam, event { eats() }).
# => TRUE
? person(Adam).
# => TRUE
